 his colleagues\". Argue that B's attitude may be more detrimental to crew cooperation than C's communication difficulty.\n\nThus we can shift recommendation to Candidate C, or at least suggest reconsideration. Provide metadata vote accordingly.\n\nLet's produce public message: \"I appreciate Agent 3's view on B, but I have concerns about B's interpersonal behavior. While B is conscientious and handles stress, the nasty remarks and weak memory for numbers could impair crew cooperation and attention to detail. In contrast, Candidate C demonstrates rapid correct decision-making and remains calm in crises\u2014critical for long-distance flights. Although C has communication difficulties and is seen as egocentric, these may be less disruptive than B's overt negativity. Therefore, I propose we consider Candidate C as the stronger overall fit.\" Vote for Candidate C.\n\nMake sure to reference Agent 3's point. Provide evidence. Then metadata."}
