his new info, perhaps by evaluating D's suitability. Since we still lack stress handling evidence, D remains uncertain. We can argue that given the lack of explicit stress handling evidence, D cannot be recommended over C. Also we can note that D's hot temper and know-it-all attitude are concerns. So we maintain recommendation for C.\n\nThus our public message: \"I note the lack of explicit stress handling data for D; while D responds adequately to unexpected events, we cannot be sure of stress resilience. Combined with D's hot temper and know-it-all, D remains less suitable than C.\" Also maybe mention that we still need reliability data for A. So we keep C.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, hot temper, know-it-all. Also mention that we still lack reliability for A.\n\nThus vote remains Candidate C.\n\nNow produce final output."}
